  "description": "<p>The University of West Alabama (UWA) is a higher-education provider in Livingston, Alabama. It provides undergraduate and postgraduate courses in over 90 fields of study. Some popular courses include Liberal Arts, Natural Sciences and Mathematics, Nursing, Technology, Business, and Education.</p><p>UWA opened in 1839 and has a long-standing reputation for providing educational opportunities to residents. But the provider has expanded to offer courses for over 4,000 students today.</p><h2>What is the University of West Alabama acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The University of West Alabama acceptance rate is 86%.</p> <p>The University of West Alabama has various top-quality resources for academic and leisure purposes. Firstly, the Julia Tutwiler Library is open seven days a week each semester and provides many resources. Books, ebooks, local archives, computers, printing services and study areas are all available.</p><p>Outside of studying, the university has several cafes and restaurants where students can meet and socialise. Young Hall Caf, Grille Works and a Subway are on-campus. In addition, UWA has a campus cinema where students can watch the latest films and attend events year-round. A fitness centre is also available to use. Here students can take part in fitness classes and use gym equipment.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>With a 13:1 student-to-teacher ratio, UWA has a close-knit community. Furthermore, the community feel at the university helps teachers to empower students to share ideas and develop academically and socially. Students are respected on campus. In addition, the university encourages students to develop in extracurricular areas. As a result, students can find many activities, clubs and organisations to join outside of class. These include outdoor activities, personalised fitness training, athletics, intramural sports, and religious and cultural clubs.</p>",
